### 3. Project Concept: AQUAVEIN-SAR

AQUAVEIN-SAR is a proposed satellite-data-based decision support platform designed to investigate Submarine Groundwater Discharge (SGD) along coastal regions.

SGD is a natural phenomenon in which groundwater from coastal aquifers enters the ocean through the seabed.

The project aims to explore potential groundwater discharge locations by evaluating satellite-derived observations and relevant environmental information.

By combining remote sensing indicators with additional hydrogeological data, AQUAVEIN-SAR aims to support the assessment of potential groundwater resources and help identify areas that may be suitable for sustainable groundwater management.

